00:00:05.590 --> 00:00:07.349 align:start position:0%
the european union extends a welcoming  hand to ukraine this week  in the hope that its government will  still fulfill the conditions needed to  sign major partnership  and trade deals ukraine has decided to  suspend preparations for signing an  association agreement  and a deep and comprehensive free trade  area pact  at the european partnership summit in  lithuania but eu leaders say the offer  a major package designed to help ukraine  survive its deep economic  problems remains on the table if kiev  meets benchmarks in three areas  the government must ensure that  elections respect international  standards  address the issue of selective justice  and make sure it doesn't happen again  and implement business reforms the eu  insists that it will not  force ukraine to choose between it and  any other regional bloc  nor does it want closer relations with  eastern partners to come at the expense  of ties with russia  but eu leaders disapprove of the  pressure  moscow has put on kiev not to sign the  agreements  the eastern partnership helps the eu to  strengthen cooperation and trade with  six countries  armenia azerbaijan georgia moldova  belarus and ukraine i am looking forward  to the eastern partnership summit in  vilnius in november  it will be an important moment for  taking important decisions for the  european union  and our eastern neighbours the summit in  vilnius is expected to see moldova and  georgia  initial their association agreements a  preliminary step  to signing them
 

